# Normalize line endings. Text files are stored with LF in the repo; Git
# converts to the platform default on checkout unless overridden below.
#
# This file exists because it did NOT: with `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for
# Windows default) and no attributes, checkout rewrites every script with CRLF.
# On Linux that makes the shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, so the kernel looks
# for an interpreter literally named "bash\r" and the run dies with
#
#     /usr/bin/env: bash<CR>: No such file or directory
#
# which a terminal renders as the unattributable ": No such file or directory"
# (the CR returns the cursor to column 0 and the rest overwrites the path).
# The rules below pin LF regardless of any machine's autocrlf setting, so a
# cluster checkout is safe even where core.autocrlf is misconfigured.
* text=auto

# These MUST stay LF even on Windows checkouts — CRLF breaks bash and make.
*.sh     text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
